# 🛡️ 13. Defensive Measures

Organizations can reduce SSH attack exposure by using:

* SSH key authentication
* Strong authentication controls
* Disabling unnecessary password authentication
* Restricting SSH access
* Monitoring authentication logs
* Rate limiting / intrusion prevention controls
* Keeping systems updated
* Using least-privilege accounts
* Monitoring privileged account activity

